a still birth is a very sad outcome for  many families  but there is a new resource for  expectant parents to help monitor your  baby  bianca holman explains books  and influencers i wanted to know it all  to make sure i have a good pregnancy and  it is overwhelming whether you are a new  or experienced parent  the pregnancy journey while thrilling  can cause anyone to worry even with  proper prenatal care and routine visits  some families are still hit by  devastating news a stillbirth  a stillbirth is a death or a loss of a  baby at or after 20 weeks of pregnancy  or during delivery this affects about  one in 160 births  that's according to the cdc the court  could wrap around the baby's neck  there are lots of different things that  could happen you can lose the amniotic  fluid  and when these things happen the baby  slows down happy birthday a non-profit  is helping to educate expecting parents  about the importance of tracking a  baby's movement  especially during the third trimester of  pregnancy the campaign in the silver  state was made possible through a  partnership with the health plan of  nevada  the count the kids campaign is an app  for mothers to monitor their bundle of  joy  to know what's normal and note any  changes mother of two  marion falvey says she used the program  during both of her pregnancies  i would you know keep track of my babies  you know how he is alive how he's doing  and staying active  um because we had a little scare at the  time  where like he had arrhythmia if it took  you  10 minutes to get 10 kicks and then all  of a sudden it takes you  an hour or an hour and a half to get  those same 10  kicks then you want to be aware of that  so instead of tracking on a piece of  paper  the app makes it easy and convenient  access at your fingertips  and if there's a sudden change in either  direction you can tell your doctor  immediately trust your mom gut because  in the end it's  it's right if you can catch a problem  at that point you can save your baby's  life  bianca holman 8 news now the user  friendly app  is available on ios and google play  stores
 

